{"title":"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(quadratic)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (quadratic)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Sequence\" title=\"Sequence\">sequence</a> of positive integers with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/0/2b02a491e6fc8db3a577b344b1a53b7a8e77e0f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/2/fe2b3a523647433bb47fc52ecc2d840fcb2e4461.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_9+a_{10}=646$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"113\" height=\"15\" /> is formed so that the first three terms are in <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Geometric_sequence\" title=\"Geometric sequence\">geometric progression</a>, the second, third, and fourth terms are in <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Arithmetic_sequence\" title=\"Arithmetic sequence\">arithmetic progression</a>, and, in general, for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/5/4553202b8409d6e88d6ca2f38c16dd00eaad74e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\ge1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"48\" height=\"15\" /> the terms <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/e/0de503cb41c1e824e259b81b770fd29795fe65d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{2n-1}, a_{2n}, a_{2n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"123\" height=\"12\" /> are in geometric progression, and the terms <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/5/9b5855e850632231e260effa538e4d7e432cd93e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{2n}, a_{2n+1},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/b/60b9a655527e0248259ccfcee34d7350fda49c14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{2n+2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> are in arithmetic progression. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1a2b6b7c193f9ba2b2134a59f1da5addcfbc98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" /> be the greatest term in this sequence that is less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/d/a4d0c7cfaf8b754ebe895f5bcb888e5d78a3caaf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+a_n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"15\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/3/d3382fa707bc4cabd1699209aa2c366ab475d5b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"10\" />; then solving for the next several terms, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/0/7802fd99c17df570abaa015c0daaaf2ebde8f775.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3 = x^2,\\ a_4 = x(2x-1),\\ a_5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"218\" height=\"19\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/4/7148582cffc2207ad84bc9d1760511c69cae3ff3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= (2x-1)^2,\\ a_6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"120\" height=\"19\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/f/09f82a4630ea33d9f27c984aec463e564d53453f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= (2x-1)(3x-2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"147\" height=\"18\" />, and in general, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/e/adeb603d224671cd374e553bf60a1cbd78c977ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{2n} = f(n-1)f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"154\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/9/bb977fc18551c2ddb768586406e3e1fd49511ba5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{2n+1} = f(n)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"108\" height=\"19\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/4/924f01d3b1eede2c1dc1fe6949103ccb538e61f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n) = nx - (n-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"158\" height=\"18\" />.<sup><span id=\"ref_1\">[<a href=\"#note_1\">1</a>]</span></sup> \n</p><p>From <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/1/67128d8e00752ca211dae7d0081675b70bd1e8f9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_9 + a_{10} = f(4)^2 + f(4)f(5) = (4x-3)(9x-7) = 646 = 2\\cdot 17 \\cdot 19\\]\" width=\"479\" height=\"19\" />, we find that by either the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadratic_formula\" title=\"Quadratic formula\">quadratic formula</a> or trial-and-error/modular arithmetic that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/c/51c80ea5862b45877f08d698a0c893bd2806a2fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/8/9b8c6b2f39cf53755c920519c0019d42dc61f633.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n) = 4n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"110\" height=\"18\" />, and we need to find the largest <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/7/9778eaf55e5fcf9136d51299786c1e53cbaa7fc4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)^2\\, \\mathrm{or}\\, f(n)f(n-1) &lt; 1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"228\" height=\"19\" />. This happens with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/f/1af843a9031c2aeb54e73855de9e565c822d513f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(7)f(8) = 29 \\cdot 33 = 957$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"193\" height=\"18\" />, and this is the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/6/5d683fd9bfc1b093103958ddb62c5146f8f041e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(8) = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"74\" height=\"18\" />th term of the sequence.\n</p><p>The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/9/619be994decfef169915f05c57e97b0165fea796.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$957 + 16 = \\boxed{973}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"131\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p><span id=\"note_1\"><a href=\"#ref_1\">^</a></span> We can show this by simultaneous <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Induction\" title=\"Induction\">induction</a>: since \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/1/f1136373caeb4ab6e85074e0d17b54e695c9c124.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}a_{2n} &amp;= 2a_{2n-1} - a_{2n-2} = 2a_{2(n-1)+1} - a_{2(n-1)} \\\\ &amp;= 2f(n-1)^2 - f(n-2)f(n-1) \\\\ &amp;= f(n-1)[2f(n-1) - f(n-2)] \\\\ &amp;= f(n-1)[(2n-2-n+2)x-(2n-4-n+3)] \\\\ &amp;= f(n-1)f(n) \\end{align*}\" width=\"416\" height=\"119\" />\nand\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/9/a190cd3da4371acbbf0f36c45bed798e9a73c889.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}a_{2n+1} &amp;= \\frac{a_{2n}^2}{a_{2n-1}} = \\frac{f(n-1)^2f(n)^2}{f(n-1)^2} = f(n)^2 \\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"324\" height=\"44\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/3/d3382fa707bc4cabd1699209aa2c366ab475d5b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"10\" />. It is apparent that the sequence grows relatively fast, so we start trying positive integers to see what <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> can be. Finding that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/3/c43970aa97091f384854d477a1e1e07356887266.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> works, after bashing out the rest of the terms we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/5/e25b151112a33c35461e97fa9daa3f30be9ae96e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{16} = 957$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/5/345f3298ec40d900ce442b777a28fa9b91488459.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{17} = 1089$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"17\" />, hence our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/9/619be994decfef169915f05c57e97b0165fea796.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$957 + 16 = \\boxed{973}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"131\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can find the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43be490b7c520eac3165135d5092e6030b5b72c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> by its bounds using three conditions:\n</p>\n<ol><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/5/2b51202880cf81b35174dd82ee0d7d1749407d58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;a_{8} = 2a_{9}-a_{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"149\" height=\"17\" /></li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/9/f593d4c5ed62adfc3d7efcefdbc5542e364b03c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{10} &lt; a_{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"15\" /> (note that the sequence must be increasing on all terms, not monotonically increasing) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/f/f5f4d79c93d6c96377051fa7c277d05e159585dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{10} &lt; \\frac{a_{10}^2}{a_{9}} \\rightarrow a_{9} &lt; a_{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"171\" height=\"44\" /></li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/7/b4739f9b4e24ad6489b7c2182d6b2e21d595c500.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{11} = \\frac{a_{10}^2}{a_{9}} = \\frac{(646-a_{9})^2}{a_{9}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"194\" height=\"44\" />, so necessarily <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43be490b7c520eac3165135d5092e6030b5b72c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> is a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/a/b1ac33b3f45c5983f2d1457a51370416f0fa64da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$646^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"17\" />, which factorizes to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc177cf472435045dc19c9e18764b0173e4dba1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^2\\cdot 17^2 \\cdot 19^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"96\" height=\"17\" /></li></ol>\n<p>Rearranging conditions 1 and 2, we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/e/f5ecefa563d261c4869443bbf9bdade8fd95ff5a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{646}{3} &lt; a_{9} &lt; \\frac{646}{2}\\]\" width=\"124\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>trying all the terms from the third condition, it is clear that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/6/386fc340ba675f6d42dc1fdec603df1e1e4b1f4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_9 = 289$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"17\" /> is the only solution. \nThen we can calculate the next few terms from there since we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/5/f659be762622558799a9119468b5008cb1b27f78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"22\" height=\"10\" /> as well, to find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/5/e25b151112a33c35461e97fa9daa3f30be9ae96e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{16} = 957$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/5/345f3298ec40d900ce442b777a28fa9b91488459.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{17} = 1089$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"17\" />, thus we have our answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/9/619be994decfef169915f05c57e97b0165fea796.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$957 + 16 = \\boxed{973}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"131\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>~KafkaTamura\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28quadratic.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(quadratic)\">Solution 4 (quadratic)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (quadratic)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/6/d26e7862b3f52ec97a48ee992b13136377738456.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2 = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"13\" />. We will write the first 10 terms in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> (this will require some rigorous polynomial division):\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\">\n<caption>First 10 Terms\n</caption>\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>Term\n</th>\n<th>Value\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />\n</td>\n<td><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e97a8af68fbc8e357d3ee0eba452022b06c1875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />\n</td>\n<td><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/2/572b65ebc3f438b176b4ca4a890799f2f72564af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />\n</td>\n<td><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76b2878564ab19b80abb21ba964abe90fe120846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" />\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/2/5e28850813a5321d2a8ae3c0510457a7337975ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />\n</td>\n<td><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/2/7f2206d08365fb12cabeacf15ad5df3a6d588ee0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x^2 - x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/5/0d5d34d49a7eb6afd4874d7bdaf23946dbf63cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />\n</td>\n<td><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/9/94984732f2c0d0a6aa11eb0d735c235978125abe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4x^2 - 4x + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"102\" height=\"18\" />\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/a/34ace040475607683853fcfd4960a8f7fa6678c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />\n</td>\n<td><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/5/3551e5c7a12f38ba45dd8cac62839b0fdfef54bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6x^2 - 7x + 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"102\" height=\"18\" />\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/2/012aa2573a77f1bfe01a31fdebe941ee94b10808.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />\n</td>\n<td><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/d/50dfbc24aad157005467fb21fde0c04f1c3dbe04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9x^2 - 12x + 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"111\" height=\"18\" />\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/a/7ead075983f8dbfa721f00c28be967778b4a6677.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" />\n</td>\n<td><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/6/8368c3a94a3c428fb2b52162fc09aa758b7100a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12x^2 - 17x + 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"120\" height=\"18\" />\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/7/fb7904c50fdc103fee44ab630f82383c0b78febc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />\n</td>\n<td><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/4/7a42b04f193b51f920d8013c1bb2c20b1ea729d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16x^2 - 24x + 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"120\" height=\"18\" />\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/5/f659be762622558799a9119468b5008cb1b27f78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"22\" height=\"10\" />\n</td>\n<td><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/8/85870e9c1ccebebea7612dd636d49038e368ad05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20x^2 - 31x + 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"129\" height=\"18\" />\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>The problem tells us that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/4/b04809b48d387f19c3e0ac07e43e5dc3b5a9f302.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_9 + a_{10} = 646,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"121\" height=\"17\" /> so we can write a quadratic and solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/1/7c1bceeac2d696a066ae32fba5b6c75a5955f788.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(16x^2 - 24x + 9) + (20x^2 - 31x + 12) = 646\\]\" width=\"345\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/5/805d6c3e55c8b02d6b9bd4f2e6b3e312f80f343e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[36x^2 - 55x + 21 = 646\\]\" width=\"177\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/e/18e336ff61a726f0268a96c1dd372a2c6c466202.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[36x^2 - 55x - 625 = 0.\\]\" width=\"172\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/2/fc2ddfe4516db662fa36804c9ec8d24b4995a484.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x = \\frac {-(-55) \\pm \\sqrt{(-55)^2 - 4(36)(-625)}}{2(36)}\\]\" width=\"310\" height=\"45\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/9/509534e093152dc51539875a1ef32bc115f5d3a0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x = \\frac {55 \\pm \\sqrt{3025 + 90000}}{72}\\]\" width=\"196\" height=\"40\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/d/a8d75f0cdc62910a9922c4b7fd77904f2ee01b8d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x = \\frac {55 \\pm \\sqrt{93025}}{72}\\]\" width=\"138\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/2/272e4bd5099ba355b7ce42e70ca950220fa56a02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac {55 \\pm 305}{72} = \\xcancel{-\\frac{125}{36}}, 5.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"200\" height=\"44\" />\n</p><p>Since every number in the series has to be a positive integer, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\nUsing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/c/51c80ea5862b45877f08d698a0c893bd2806a2fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> we can find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/7/fb7904c50fdc103fee44ab630f82383c0b78febc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/5/f659be762622558799a9119468b5008cb1b27f78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"22\" height=\"10\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/6/4d66007827d507e0734a1ead449c5fc753245686.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_9 = 16(5)^2 - 24(5) + 9 = 16(25) - 120 + 9 = 400 - 120 + 9 = 289.\\]\" width=\"527\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/2/382d04e0939285193de8bfa2574381847ba01daf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_{10} = 20(5)^2 - 31(5) + 12 = 20(25) - 155 + 12 = 500 - 155 + 12 = 357.\\]\" width=\"537\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><br />\nNotice that our arithmetic differences are increasing by 16: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/f/b8f567ede23477347ced3eb89e9753d49962a99d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20 \\rightarrow 36 \\rightarrow 52 \\rightarrow 68...$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"175\" height=\"14\" /> So following this pattern, the next differences will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/f/b0f207e0623d1287507306203bb6bae74e0b0fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$84, 100, 116$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"91\" height=\"17\" />. \n</p><p>The geometric ratios follow a pattern of adding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to the numerator and denominator: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/255ae74854d94a848e4f1f88be9a459d84d13834.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{9}{5} \\rightarrow \\frac{13}{9} \\rightarrow \\frac{17}{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"116\" height=\"38\" />. The next ratios will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/5/dc574d541ca4278748a923f868e97697b156ceb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{21}{17}, \\frac{25}{21}, \\frac{29}{25}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"90\" height=\"38\" /> \n</p><p>We have everything we need to calculate the next few terms:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/7/e07e956f27e410886ace2f8abb02657a08d89784.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{11} = 357 \\cdot \\frac{21}{17} = 441,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"169\" height=\"38\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/e/32e54f0564df73c4dca3ff60045f1ee1e5ebb652.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{12} = 441 + 84 = 525,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"174\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/7/8e790bae0c516de9fce1a3db34ce1f09d40b73f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{13} = 525 \\cdot \\frac{25}{21} = 625,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"169\" height=\"38\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/e/1ee1a6204748d838114857059884482c7d547486.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{14} = 625 + 100 = 725,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"183\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/4/6b451903a0190e97dce7feea30450d508719bfae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{15} = 725 \\cdot \\frac{29}{25} = 841,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"169\" height=\"38\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/c/93c0315a4e99b68e2ab6db87b5d71610015636c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{16} = 841 + 116 = 957.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"183\" height=\"17\" />\nWe stop here because it's clear the next term will exceed 1000. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/4/0f469b6534f823edfd551c9c176218e1512f01b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{16} = 957,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"82\" height=\"17\" /> the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/1/9b11df3e208d1f6f0bc0a25d4ea04eb301badbc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$957 + 16 = \\boxed{973}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"137\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Grogg007\" title=\"User:Grogg007\">grogg007</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II\" title=\"2004 AIME II\">2004 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2004 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2004\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017202801\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.066 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.096 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 598/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1961/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 135/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 18372/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   44.337      1 -total\n 21.76%    9.646      1 Template:Ref\n 18.83%    8.349      1 Template:AIME_box\n 16.58%    7.353      1 Template:Note\n 12.17%    5.395      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:2696:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017202801 and revision id 255953. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}